---
import TextPage from "../layouts/TextPage.astro";
import { pageMeta } from "../lib/seo";
import { BRAND_OWNERS, CONTACT_EMAIL, OWNER_NAME, SITE_NAME } from "../lib/site";

const meta = pageMeta("about");
---

<TextPage
  searchable
  title={meta.title}
  h1={meta.h1}
  description={meta.description}
  intro={`${SITE_NAME} is an independent price guide for used electronics in Canada.`}
>
  <h2>What it is</h2>
  <p>
    Used electronics are listed at very different prices, and it is hard to tell a good price from an ordinary one. {SITE_NAME}
    collects public listings from Facebook Marketplace across Canada and turns them into a clear picture for each model: what
    people are asking on average, how that has moved over time, and which current listings are priced well below the market.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone buying or selling a used phone or laptop who wants to know what a fair asking price is before they message a seller
    or post a listing.
  </p>

  <h2>What it is not</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      It is not a marketplace. We do not sell anything, hold any items or take payments. Every listing links back to Facebook,
      where the seller and the buyer deal directly.
    </li>
    <li>It shows asking prices, not sold prices, and it does not check whether a listing is still available.</li>
    <li>
      It is not connected to {BRAND_OWNERS}. Those names are trademarks of their owners and are used only to describe
      the listings and products we track.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who runs it</h2>
  <p>{SITE_NAME} is an independent project run by {OWNER_NAME}. You can read exactly how the numbers are built on the <a href="/how-it-works/">How it works</a> page.</p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>Found a mistake or have a question? Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> or see the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.</p>
</TextPage>
